<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australia unions not inflation threat - Fraser.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australia unions not inflation threat - Fraser.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Bernie Fraser said on Thursday that Australia's more open economy, lower union coverage and higher unemployment meant any union push for higher wages under the new conservative government was unlikely to endanger the low inflation outlook.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it's these fundamental factors that hopefully mean that we'll continue to experience moderate wage increases, low inflation and a minimum of industrial disruption,&quot; Fraser said in Tokyo after a BZW Australia Day address.</p>
<p>His comments were relayed by Reuters Financial Television (RFTV).</p>
</text>
